<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50012" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ū^trĭcŭlus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		dim.
		uterus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, in gen., <i>the
			belly</i>, <i>abdomen</i>, of bees, <i><span class="en">Plin. 11,
				12, 12, § 31</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Esp., <i>a little
			womb</i> or <i>matrix</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 11,
				37, 84, § 209</span></i>; <i><span class="en">30, 14, 43, §
			124</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of plants, <i>a
			bud</i> or <i>calycle</i> of a flower, <i>a hull</i> or <i>husk</i> of grain,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				16, 25, 39, § 94</span></i>; <i><span class="en">18, 11, 29, §
			115</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
